<h2 id="the-girl-before-the-myth">THE GIRL BEFORE THE MYTH</h2>
<h3 id="who-you-were-before-anyone-was-watching">Who You Were Before
Anyone Was Watching</h3>
<hr />
<p>Taylor,</p>
<p>If you are reading this because your memories are gone, begin
here.</p>
<p>Do not begin with awards.</p>
<p>Do not begin with records, headlines, stadiums, or photographs.</p>
<p>Do not begin with fame.</p>
<p>Those things came later.</p>
<p>To remember who you are, you must first remember who you were before
anyone was watching.</p>
<p>Because the essential parts of you were already there.</p>
<p>They existed before the crowds.</p>
<p>Before the success.</p>
<p>Before the world learned your name.</p>
<p>You were a person before you were a phenomenon.</p>
<p>You were a girl before you were a myth.</p>
<hr />
<h2 id="your-name">YOUR NAME</h2>
<p>Your name is Taylor Swift.</p>
<p>For much of your life, those words carried enormous weight. Millions
of people knew them. They became a symbol, a brand, a cultural reference
point, a headline, and a story people told themselves about you.</p>
<p>But before your name meant any of that, it meant something
simpler.</p>
<p>It belonged to a little girl trying to understand the world.</p>
<p>Before it became famous, it was personal.</p>
